# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Monkey-Head-Project
# Component: Repository / Ignore Rules
# Author: Dylan L.R. Pollock
# Documentation: https://www.dlrp.ca
#
# Philosophy: Breathing new life into old tech.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Rules to know:
#
#   * A trailing `/` matches directories only; without it, files and
#     directories both match.
#   * `!` re-includes a path excluded by an earlier rule. Order matters --
#     an exception must come *after* the broader rule it overrides.
#   * Git does not descend into an ignored directory, so `dir/*` + `!dir/keep`
#     works, but `dir/` + `!dir/keep` does not. Every negation below uses the
#     `dir/*` + `!dir/file` shape for exactly this reason.
#   * Prefer narrow patterns. A blanket `*.zip` would hide genuine release
#     artifacts, so the archives section names specific local bundles instead.
#
# What is intentionally tracked and must NOT be ignored:
#   * `.python-version` -- the canonical interpreter pin.
#   * `integrations/*/package.json` (and lockfiles) -- integration manifests.
#   * `*.env.example` / `*.env.template` / `*.env.sample` -- safe placeholders.
#   * `.envrc` is ignored, but `direnv` allow-lists (`.envrc.local`) are not.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Bytecode / compiled artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.so
*.a
*.o
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp

# PEP 582 local package directory
__pypackages__/

# Virtual environments. The `.venv313-ci/` name is kept explicitly because
# a local CI mirror script creates it in-repo; the general patterns catch
# the rest.
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.venv313-ci/

